From 87f469c5a1f00eb499830bc96b67d3c6a58f1e7a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:38:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(layout): allow scrolling columns wider than the output

A scrolling column's extent could never exceed one viewport, so no window
could span two screens and be panned through. The ceiling lived in the parse
ranges, the keybind argument bounds, the setters, and the pixel resolve; the
strip, gestures, and snapshots already handle a strip longer than the output.

widthFrac for scrolling columns now runs 0.1 to 4.0 (kMaxWideFraction):
extent_presets, default_extent_fraction, default_scrolling_extent[_px], and
window-set-* accept it, non-scrolling layouts clamp through
Layout::maxExtentFraction, and floating preset cycles skip steps they cannot
realize. A wide column pans through layout-scroll-* and layout-scroll-drag,
strip swipes rest at either edge, refocusing keeps the pan in place, and
resize grows to the same ceiling. A client-chosen first width stays one tile;
wider extents come from rules, window-set-*, and resize.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
